# Security AppSec (Auto)

Defers to `00-core-fsm` Safety on conflict. This file is the SharePoint-concrete digest.

## Secrets
- Never hardcode credentials, API keys, tokens, tenant IDs, or connection strings
- Never commit `.env` or tenant secrets
- Never log passwords, tokens, or session identifiers

## Input / Output
- Sanitize all input; escape all output (HTML attribute/text/URL contexts)
- No `eval`, unchecked `innerHTML` / `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with user data, or shell `exec` on user data
- Prefer textContent / safe DOM APIs over raw HTML injection

## AuthZ
- Data R/W = list/item permissions — AuthN success is not enough (IDOR)
- Prefer host SharePoint auth / existing services over custom in-page auth
- Least privilege for admin/script surfaces

## Dependencies
- Do not add packages without user approval (`00` Dependencies)
- Data SoT this repo = `SPHttpClient`. `@pnp/sp` = ask-first only

## PII
- Treat user names, emails, scores, and participant identity as sensitive
- No PII in front-end globals, HTML comments, or chat dumps

## Do not
- Weaken security “to make it sound less serious”
- Touch production secrets or expose Local/tenant credentials in replies
